From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FAROVITUS <farovitus@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:07:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] release: enable buffer stuffing recovery and battery
 broadcast rate limit

My zeroflte build (Exynos 7420, Lineage 22.2) runs into both problems
these Android 16 flags fix, and the code behind them is already in the
22.2 tree, only switched off.

android.view.flags.buffer_stuffing_recovery: SurfaceFlinger already
reports the queued buffer count of a stuffed ViewRootImpl layer in the
vsync event, and Choreographer already reacts to it, but ViewRootImpl only
marks its layer recoverable when the flag is on. Without it a single late
frame in a continuous animation leaves one extra buffer queued for good:
UiBench RenderingJitter sits at 4 refreshes of latency (Total about 36 ms,
dequeue about 11 ms) instead of 3 (about 18.5 ms) while SurfaceFlinger
presents every frame on time.

com.android.server.flags.rate_limit_battery_changed_broadcast:
BatteryService broadcasts ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED for every new millivolt.
On this phone each broadcast costs SystemUI tens of milliseconds of CPU on
the small cores and a status bar frame miss. With the flag, a voltage-only
change is sent only when it moved at least 1 % and 20 s have passed, and a
temperature-only change only when it moved at least 1 degree C.

Both are fixed read-only flags, so this takes a framework rebuild. Not
built or tested yet.

Signed-off-by: FAROVITUS <farovitus@gmail.com>
---
 release/aconfig/bp1a/Android.bp                            | 2 ++
 release/aconfig/bp1a/android.view.flags/Android.bp         | 7 +++++++
 .../buffer_stuffing_recovery_flag_values.textproto         | 6 ++++++
 release/aconfig/bp1a/com.android.server.flags/Android.bp   | 7 +++++++
 ...e_limit_battery_changed_broadcast_flag_values.textproto | 6 ++++++
